{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1114702-sleeper-witnesses","id":1114702,"title":"Sleeper witnesses.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-11T12:16:20-07:00","id":1114702,"title":"Sleeper witnesses.","content":"For a mage to get that +5 diff due to sleeper witnesses; a sleeper must DIRECTLY see the reality being broken, they need to witness something that opposes any common sense that they might possess, right?<br /> They basically need to witness the willworking of the magic, for an example spawning flames out of nowhere, etc.<br /> <br /> I play a game with a few buddies, where I ended up burning a forest with forces 4. I made sure there were no sleepers around when i cast the effect, no sleeper ever witnessed me willworking the magic. However, according to someone, after the fire spread sleepers from town could see the fire, and he says that it counts as sleeper witnesses lol. But all they see is fire, nothing reality-breaking happened from the sleepers' perspective, I mean for all they know a random arsonist could've brought the forest up in flames. They wouldn't assume it was done in a supernatural manner. Not to mention that NO SLEEPER ever witnessed my mage willworking the magic, I was alone.<br /> <br /> I need to know who's in right here, Myself (The caster of the magic) or the other party that claims that even if sleepers see the effect AFTER it was cast (and when it was cast there weren't sleepers) it still counts as sleeper witnesses, which is totally ridiculous IMO cuz afaik a sleeper needs to actually witness the mage willworking the magic and see them pulling off some chants, spawning fire out of thin air etc or anything else that opposes any sort of common sense. Something that from the sleeper's perspective cannot be done, needs to be done right in front of him to get that +5 diff, right? Cause then basically u break reality RIGHT in front of a sleeper, and it clashes with his beliefs (which in this case are that he doesnt believe in magic) and hence the reality takes his side and makes it harder on the mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","user":"MowtekPvP","date":". 07-11-2017, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T12:32:56-07:00","id":1114704,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I side with you on this. Vulgarity and witnesses should be based on the casting and the immediate result, not the eventual consequences.<br /> Otherwise you can have all sorts of innocuous things become vulgar with witnesses.<br /> For example, running into an empty restroom to transform into a dog. If people see you, then see dog you running out, but then go in the restroom and don't see anyone at all, is that suddenly vulgar with witnesses rather than just vulgar?<br /> <br /> If it is vulgar with witnesses regardless, then what's the point of running into the restroom at all, might as well turn into a dog right before their eyes as far as difficulty is concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-11-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T12:33:15-07:00","id":1114705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1114702-sleeper-witnesses#post1114702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Was the magic just setting the fire, or was it actually involved in the fire when it was seen? I.e. was your magic 'creating a forest fire ex nihilo' or was it 'setting a part of the forest alight, whcih then burned to the point that it was seen'?<br /> <br /> In the former case, the other party is right, IMO, in the latter, you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T12:37:37-07:00","id":1114707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1114702-sleeper-witnesses?p=1114705#post1114705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was the magic just setting the fire, or was it actually involved in the fire when it was seen? I.e. was your magic 'creating a forest fire ex nihilo' or was it 'setting a part of the forest alight, whcih then burned to the point that it was seen'?<br /> <br /> In the former case, the other party is right, IMO, in the latter, you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>the later case, I burnt a certain portion and it spread.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I appreciate the quick answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","user":"MowtekPvP","date":". 07-11-2017, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T12:37:37-07:00","id":1114708,"title":"","content":"Accidentally double posted, my bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T17:30:38-07:00","id":1114825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1114702-sleeper-witnesses?p=1114707#post1114707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the later case, I burnt a certain portion and it spread.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I appreciate the quick answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you did or did not create the fire ex nihilo? If the former, it's Vulgar without witnesses, if the latter then it's probably Coincidental. You used existing fire to spread it into a forest-destroying inferno. Forest fires happen all the time, so there's no reason for witnesses, hypothetical or otherwise, to see anything amiss.<br /> <br /> Not that people witnessing the Effect after the fact would actually make it Vulgar with witnesses in either case. Remember, other than with Botches (which are a whole other matter), there's no mechanical difference between witnessed vulgarity and non-witnesses vulgarity, when the Effect is already underway. At least in 2nd Ed and M20, you get 1 Paradox for any kind of Vulgar Effect. The only other difference between With and Without is difficulty number. And it's not reasonable for the player or storyteller to retroactively take away successes from a previous roll, because the difficulty would have been higher. No one can be expected to keep track of the exact results of their die roll from five, ten, fifteen minutes before. Most times, only the presence of 10s, 1s, and the number of dice that meet the difficulty are paid attention to; the exact values are irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 07-11-2017, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T18:35:16-07:00","id":1115747,"title":"","content":"Is the penalty really +5 now? That is incredibly dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T19:49:27-07:00","id":1115760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1114702-sleeper-witnesses?p=1115747#post1115747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the penalty really +5 now? That is incredibly dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always been +5.<br /> <br /> Subtle magic is Base Diff: Highest Sphere +3<br /> Vulgar magic is Base Diff: Highest Sphere +4<br /> Vulgar with Witnesses Base Diff: Highest Sphere +5<br /> <br /> When has that not been the case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T23:30:23-07:00","id":1115821,"title":"","content":"You're right, my mistake. I always thought of it as +2 because I didn't count the base +3 for Coincidental magic. So in my you add the base (+3) plus Sphere, plus 1 or 2 for vulgar or vulgar with witnesses respectively. When I saw &quot;+5&quot; I was actually thinking &quot;Sphere +8.&quot; My subconscious is dumb, and I am dumb for not questioning it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 07-14-2017, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:34:11-07:00","id":1118919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1114702-sleeper-witnesses?p=1115821#post1115821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, my mistake. I always thought of it as +2 because I didn't count the base +3 for Coincidental magic. So in my you add the base (+3) plus Sphere, plus 1 or 2 for vulgar or vulgar with witnesses respectively. When I saw &quot;+5&quot; I was actually thinking &quot;Sphere +8.&quot; My subconscious is dumb, and I am dumb for not questioning it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I understand, it wasn't even a <i>penalty</i> as such, as it didn't count against the maximum modifier divergence from the base difficulty (which is \u00b13).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T22:43:57-07:00","id":1119421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1114702-sleeper-witnesses?p=1118919#post1118919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understand, it wasn't even a <i>penalty</i> as such, as it didn't count against the maximum modifier divergence from the base difficulty (which is \u00b13).</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. It was just the way I had conceptualized it without really thinking about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}